Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||10-05-1999||01:21 AM||||Not sure about ones that size, but I can get 1000 3.5" x 2" (normal card size) business cards printed for about $100 CDN plus shipping.. full color, glossy paper. <P>Check around, some places print post card-size cards, that might be a better solution. I still like my idea of printing them on normal paper and laminating them.. it'd be cheap and they'd stand up in the rain better than ones with just paper. (plus they'd look like they cost more than they did!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Might look like you were offering the person some sort of membership or something.. I dunno, just a thought)<p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 10-05-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gokart||10-05-1999||07:12 AM||||DaRkLoRD, That's exactly what I did last night! I didn't have any laminate, so I used clear packaging tape. Looks like laminate! ||||reg||14
Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||10-05-1999||03:23 PM||||There's a place in my town that charges about $1 or less for a sheet. Not sure how many of those cards you coult fit on a sheet of paper, but if you could get 4 on, it'd be about a quarter to get each one laminated. not the peel and stick stuff, I mean the way where it's put thru a machine and melts plastic around the paper. I think most copy places do that, as well as some office supply stores. They might even offer printing services, tho I've never checked.||||reg||1
